\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
If every sphere homeomorphism conformal off the boundary of a circle domain D is a Mobius map, must every conformal bijection from D to another circle domain be the restriction of a Mobius map?

\subsection{Short English statement}
If every sphere homeomorphism conformal off the boundary of a circle domain D is a Mobius map, must every conformal bijection from D to another circle domain be the restriction of a Mobius map?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://www.math.stonybrook.edu/~bishop/classes/math536.S24/He_Schramm_1993.pdf}.
\item[S2] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
